<title>FRANCE: French union cancels strikes due to election.</title>
<headline>French union cancels strikes due to election.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The leader of France's independent Force Ouvriere union said he was calling off two planned demonstrations so as not to interfere with a parliamentary election next month.</p>
<p>He said a strike in the banking sector set for May 15 and a demonstration in Paris and Toulouse planned for May 28 were being cancelled.</p>
<p>&quot;There is an old tradition that unions always hesitate to mount protests during electoral periods so as to avoid being manipulated, taken over or used,&quot; Blondel told Radio Classique in an interview.</p>
<p>President Jacques Chirac dissolved the National Assembly on Monday and called a two-round parliamentary election for May 25 and June 1.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
